@startuml
title MatrixRTC Call Token Authorization
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Element client" as Client
participant "Nginx edge" as Edge
participant "Synapse call-policy guard" as Guard
participant "Keycloak policy snapshot" as Policy
participant "Synapse room state" as State
participant "Synapse MatrixRTC proxy / appservice" as RTCProxy
participant "Private LiveKit JWT service" as JWT
participant "LiveKit SFU" as SFU

alt Native Matrix Client-Server token request
  Client -> Edge : POST MSC4195 get_token\nMatrix bearer + room/call data
  Edge -> Guard : fixed internal guard route
  Guard -> Guard : authenticate bearer; derive user from token
  Guard -> Policy : load current room-policy grant
  Guard -> State : check joined membership, Megolm and call power >= 10
  Guard -> Guard : require current writer-level room authorization
  Guard -> RTCProxy : POST fixed native get_token route\nforward original bearer + request
  RTCProxy -> JWT : MatrixRTC application-service request
  JWT -> State : validate room membership / Matrix token
  JWT --> RTCProxy : candidate call JWT
  RTCProxy --> Guard : candidate token response
  Guard -> Policy : reload current policy
  Guard -> State : recheck authorization after token mint
  Guard -> Edge : return only validated JWT
  Edge --> Client : Matrix token response
else Element Call SFU token request
  Client -> Edge : POST /livekit/jwt/sfu/get\nOpenID proof + room/call data
  Edge -> Guard : fixed internal guard route
  Guard -> State : validate OpenID proof using local userinfo
  Guard -> Policy : load current room-policy grant
  Guard -> State : check joined membership, Megolm and call power >= 10
  Guard -> JWT : fixed private /sfu/get request
  JWT -> State : validate Matrix OpenID / room membership
  JWT --> Guard : candidate URL + JWT
  Guard -> Policy : reload current policy
  Guard -> State : recheck room state and call permission
  Guard --> Edge : return candidate only if still authorized
  Edge --> Client : authorized URL + call token
end

Client -> SFU : HTTPS/WSS signaling with call token
Client -> SFU : media transport (network dependent)

note over Edge,JWT
  Other public JWT mint routes are denied. The federation
  get_token route is not exposed in this single-homeserver demo.
  Synapse's standalone OpenID userinfo route is narrowly exposed
  for proof validation; the general federation API is not enabled.
end note

note bottom
  This diagram describes token authorization and signaling.
  It does not establish successful media transport, client
  compatibility, or ringing. Test audio/video, NAT, firewall,
  and TURN behavior for the selected clients and deployment.
end note
@enduml
